INTERFACE
• How to implement an interface:
class name extends superclass implements interface1, interface2{
// class-body
}
• All the non-static and non-default method specified in the interface must be implemented in
any of the concrete classes that implements the interface.
• All the implemented methods must be declared as public. (all abstract methods in interfaces
are public, so we cannot reduce the visibilit y )
• Return type and the input parameters must match the specification.

